comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-10T23:16:46.855Z",codex-gpt5,"Implementation evidence: search rendering extraction remains in the broad docstring bundle; shared list/search timestamp predicates removed the final cross-command clone without changing filter semantics. pnpm typecheck, pnpm lint (0 clones), and focused search/list regression suites passed."
  "2026-07-11T00:02:35.336Z",codex-gpt5,"Scope boundary: this PR extracted search rendering and shared list/search timestamp filtering, reducing duplication to zero, but query-parsing and inline-field extraction remain outstanding and the acceptance target of <=1500 LOC per module is not yet met. Returning the item to open so only actively worked items remain in_progress."
  "2026-09-19T16:29:59.265Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: original files fully inspected before extraction. Public compatibility exports and test hooks retained; no cap or coverage threshold raised. Search and CLI focused baseline 272 tests passed before and after extraction. Infrastructure now additionally separates native SDK action dispatch/schema, manifest parsing/registration validation, and all three completion renderers. Full quality and coverage validation in progress."
  "2026-09-19T17:01:12.443Z","harness:codex","Linked verification passed for both registered search/list and BM25/default-mode/relevance suites. Full temporary-project acceptance completed 17 steps including init, package activation, create/claim, comments/notes/files, exact-ID/count/highlighted linked-content searches, three shell completions, structured close/release and history/resolution validation. Search and all infrastructure ownership modules remain below their item acceptance caps."
  "2026-09-19T17:10:28.068Z","harness:codex","Final coverage: 9057 tests across 717 files pass; statements 64759/64759, branches 49447/49447, functions 13457/13457, lines 61969/61969. Exact zero-uncovered gate passes 100/100/100/100. Search orchestration is 697 effective lines; largest search module is 1151 physical lines. Ten fixed-time golden result envelopes are byte-identical; linked search/list/relevance tests pass. Implementation closure is prepared on the review branch; hosted checks and merge remain delivery follow-up."
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-11T02:51:12.677Z",maintainer-agent,"Scope update after PR#506 (2026-07-11): the rendering slice is PARTIALLY done — search-rendering.ts extracted (137 lines) but search.ts is now 3740 physical / ~3330 effective lines (the static gate now counts only non-empty non-comment lines, changed in PR#506 to avoid penalizing docstrings — title's \"3119/3400\" numbers predate both changes). Effective count sits at ~98% of the 3400 cap, so this file is still one feature away from failing the gate. Remaining scope per PR#506 tracker note: query-parser + inline-field decomposition (keep the two parse layers' order from PR#290 intact). Suggested order: (1) inline field:value layer out first — it is the most self-contained and owns the list.ts:489 cross-file clone site; (2) query parser; (3) sweep remaining render helpers into search-rendering.ts."
  "2026-07-13T09:49:55.267Z",maintainer-agent,"Scope refresh 2026-07-13 (review pass #78): search.ts is now 3359 gate-normalized LOC (98.8% of the 3400 cap) — grown from the 3119 (92%) in this item's title. ~40 lines of headroom; any non-trivial search feature lands over the cap. Split urgency now on par with main.ts (see pm-yh8r census note of same date)."
  "2026-09-19T16:46:02.483Z","harness:codex","September architecture decision: CLI search was already a thin SDK adapter, so complete the historical decomposition in SDK query ownership. Keep parsing order and explicit-option precedence in input/filters, lexical scoring/highlights in lexical, linked/vector corpus work in corpus/semantic, and projections in response. Preserve public search exports and test seams. Ten fixed-time complete JSON golden configurations matched the original byte for byte; no consumer migration is required."
